"""Option labels in nine languages.

Written side by side rather than as nine files, and that is deliberate: an
option's nine labels have to mean the same thing, and the only way to keep them
meaning the same thing is to be able to see them together. Nine separate files
drift the first time somebody edits one of them.

`en hi bn ta te mr gu kn pa` — the order is `LANGUAGES`, and the emitter asserts
every row has nine entries, so a short row is a build failure rather than a
silently missing label.

**Patient-facing wording, not dictionary wording.** `heaviness` after a meal is
"भारीपन", the word somebody would use about their own stomach, not a clinical
term for the sensation.
"""

